window.pandaSearch = [{"title": "Overview", "href": "index.html", "text": " \n \n    Python library for molecular simulation \n   From density to contact angle \n   PANDA fits analytical models to one-dimensional density profiles of confined liquids. Estimate a contact angle, identify plausible interface shapes, and compare results across trajectory blocks. \n   Run the quick start \u2192  \n    \n   Synthetic slit-pore roll \u00b7 fitted \u03b8 = 120.61\u00b0  \n \n  Start with your data \n \n  Try a synthetic profile \u2192  Recover a known angle in a slit pore in a few lines of Python.  \n  Analyze a trajectory \u2192  Load simulation frames, compute density, and fit blocks.  \n  Use the command line \u2192  Run the same workflow with shell commands or a TOML file.  \n    What PANDA supports \n The name stands for Predicting Angle from Nanoscale Density Analysis. The library covers slit, triangular, square, and cylindrical pores. The  shape catalog  identifies which models can fit density and which supply surface terms for stability diagrams. \n Explore the related  PANDA Polygon  geometry models and the  PANDA Dynamic  two-angle method.  "}, {"title": "Installation", "href": "installation.html", "text": "The package is named panda-md, the Python module is panda_md, and the shell command is panda.   Install from source \n Use Python 3.10 or newer. This manual targets the developer repository\u2019s 0.1.0 alpha API. The source checkout requires repository access. \n  Shell   git clone https://github.com/Ilya-Garanov-WorkingAcc/PANDA_2.0.git   \n  Shell   cd PANDA_2.0\npython -m venv .venv   \n Activate the environment with  source .venv/bin/activate  on macOS or Linux, or  .venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1  in PowerShell. \n  Shell   python -m pip install .   \n   Optional dependencies \n From the same checkout, install the  md  extra for trajectory input and  plot  for Matplotlib figures. \n  Shell   python -m pip install &quot;.[md,plot]&quot;      Check the installation   Python    import  panda_md\n\n print ( &quot;PANDA import OK&quot; )     Output   PANDA import OK    Run  panda --help  in a shell to list the available commands.  "}, {"title": "Quick start", "href": "quickstart.html", "text": "Generate a noisy slit-pore roll profile with a known angle, then fit it with PANDA.   Generate and fit a profile \n The slit is 8 nm wide. The synthetic model uses \u03b8 = 120\u00b0, a layer thickness of 0.03 times the slit width, and a liquid volume fraction of 0.40. \n  Python    from  panda_md  import  SlitPore, synthetic_profile\n\npore = SlitPore(width_nm= 8.0 , length_nm= 16.0 )\nroll = pore.interface( &quot;roll&quot; )\ntruth = { &quot;theta&quot; :  120.0 ,  &quot;delta&quot; :  0.03 ,  &quot;phi&quot; :  0.40 }\nprofile = synthetic_profile(\n    roll, truth, density_bulk_per_nm3= 30.0 ,\n    noise_std= 0.005 , seed= 0 ,\n)\nresult = roll.fit(\n    profile, optimize=[ &quot;theta&quot; ,  &quot;delta&quot; ], density_bulk_per_nm3= 30.0 ,\n)\n print ( f&quot;theta = {result.values[&#x27;theta&#x27;]:.2f} deg&quot; )\n print ( f&quot;delta/H = {result.values[&#x27;delta&#x27;]:.4f}&quot; )\n print ( f&quot;phi = {result.values[&#x27;phi&#x27;]:.4f}&quot; )\n print ( f&quot;L1 loss = {result.loss:.5f}&quot; )\n print (result.problems())     Output   theta = 120.61 deg\ndelta/H = 0.0301\nphi = 0.4002\nL1 loss = 0.00377\n()      Read the result \n These values come from the archived run for this example. PANDA optimizes \u03b8 and \u03b4. It derives \u03c6 from the profile using the supplied bulk density. The last line is the list of fit flags. \n  Download the Python example  \u00b7  Download the normalized profile and fit  \n   Plot the fit and residuals \n With the  plot  extra installed, run this cell after fitting. The residual is the observed normalized density minus the fitted curve at each bin. \n  Python    import  matplotlib.pyplot  as  plt\n from  panda_md.plotting  import  plot_fit\n\nfig, (fit_ax, residual_ax) = plt.subplots(\n     2 ,  1 , sharex= True , height_ratios=( 2 ,  1 ), layout= &quot;constrained&quot; \n)\nplot_fit(result, ax=fit_ax)\nfit_ax.set_xlabel( &quot;&quot; )\nresidual_ax.axhline( 0 , color= &quot;0.5&quot; , linewidth= 1 )\nresidual_ax.plot(result.coordinate, result.data - result.model_curve,  &quot;.&quot; , markersize= 3 )\nresidual_ax. set (xlabel= &quot;Reduced coordinate, z/H&quot; , ylabel= &quot;Data \u2212 fit&quot; )\nfig.savefig( &quot;roll-fit.png&quot; , dpi= 150 )\nplt.show()      Plot from the archived synthetic roll fit.  Download PNG .     Use your own data \n Follow the  trajectory guide  for simulation output. If you already have a density profile, see  fitting a saved profile .  "}, {"title": "Pores and shapes", "href": "geometries.html", "text": "A pore defines the confinement geometry. A named shape defines the analytical interface inside it.   Set up a pore \n \n     Slit   SlitPore  Wall-to-wall width  H    \n     Triangle   TrianglePore  Side length  a    \n     Square   SquarePore  Side length  a    \n     Cylinder   CylinderPore  Tube diameter  D    \n \n Choose a pore to open its  3D shape gallery . \n  pore.interface(\"roll\")  selects an analytical model for the slit. Polygon names encode the number of walls touched ( w ) and corners occupied ( c ). \n   Shape catalog \n This snapshot lists 26 shapes. Of these, 18 supply a density profile and 24 supply surface terms. Availability describes the implemented formulas. Check the individual angle and volume-fraction limits before fitting. \n \n Pore   All pores  Slit  Triangle  Square  Cylinder   \n Operation   All operations  Density profile  Surface terms   \n   \n     Pore  Shape  Density profile  Surface terms      Slit   droplet   Yes  Yes    Slit   roll   Yes  Yes    Slit   worm   Yes  Yes    Slit   layer   Yes  Yes    Slit   doughnut   Yes  \u2014    Slit   perforation   Yes  \u2014    Triangle   capsule_w3c0   Yes  Yes    Triangle   droplet_w1c0   Yes  Yes    Triangle   filament_w0c0   Yes  Yes    Triangle   filament_w3c0   Yes  Yes    Triangle   droplet_w2c0   \u2014  Yes    Triangle   droplet_w3c0   \u2014  Yes    Triangle   filament_w0c0_straight   \u2014  Yes    Triangle   filament_w1c0   \u2014  Yes    Triangle   filament_w2c0   \u2014  Yes    Triangle   filament_w2c1   \u2014  Yes    Triangle   filament_w3c1   \u2014  Yes    Triangle   filament_w3c2   \u2014  Yes    Square   capsule_w4c0   Yes  Yes    Square   droplet_w1c0   Yes  Yes    Square   droplet_w2c0   Yes  Yes    Square   droplet_w2c1   Yes  Yes    Square   filament_w0c0   Yes  Yes    Square   filament_w0c0_straight   Yes  Yes    Square   filament_w1c0   Yes  Yes    Cylinder   capsule   Yes  Yes     \n Run  panda shapes --pore triangle  to see the installed version\u2019s models, parameter bounds, and regimes. \n   Limits of the models \n Slit and cylindrical contact-angle models cover the non-wetting side of 90\u00b0. Some polygon models have narrower domains. Models such as a flat  layer  have no contact-angle parameter. Check  model.is_feasible(...)  and  model.phi_limits(...)  for the specific shape.    Examples   Fit a triangular filament   "}, {"title": "3D shape gallery", "href": "shape-gallery.html", "text": "Explore interface morphologies in slit, triangular, square, and cylindrical pores.   Check the package capabilities  for density fitting and surface terms. Cards marked \u201cFormula draft\u201d show geometries from the research formulas.  Graphite marks the solid walls, dark brown the wetting phase, and blue the non-wetting phase. The contact angle is measured through the blue phase. The volume fraction refers to the full pore, including for cutaway views.  Slit      doughnut   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.28  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB       droplet   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.10  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB       layer   \u03c6 = 0.48  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB       perforation   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.77  In package catalog \u00b7 Cutaway   View in 3D  Download GLB       roll   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.54  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB       worm   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.20  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB     Triangle      filament_w0c0   \u03c6 = 0.28  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB       filament_w1c0   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.30  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB       filament_w2c0   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.31  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB       filament_w3c0   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.70  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB       filament_w2c1   \u03b8 = 110\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.39  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB       filament_w3c2   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.70  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB       filament_w3c1   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.70  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB       droplet_w1c0   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.07  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB       droplet_w2c0   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.08  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB       droplet_w3c0   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.14  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB       droplet_w2c1   \u03b8 = 110\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.06  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB       filament_w0c0_straight   \u03c6 = 0.46  In package catalog   View in 3D  Download GLB       capsule_w3c3   \u03b8 = 115\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.53  Formula draft \u00b7 Cutaway   View in 3D  Download GLB       capsule_w3c0   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.37  In package catalog \u00b7 Cutaway   View in 3D  Download GLB     Square      layerx   \u03c6 = 0.38  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB       layerxs   \u03c6 = 0.49  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB       wormx_1   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.37  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB       wormx_4   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.74  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB       wormx_angle_1_4   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.79  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB       wormx_angle_2_4   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.83  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB       wormx_angle_3_4   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.74  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB       wormx_angle_2_3   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.53  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB       wormx_2_opp   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.58  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB       wormx_angle_1   \u03b8 = 125\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.43  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB       droplet_1   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.15  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB       droplet_2   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.18  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB       droplet_angle_2   \u03b8 = 125\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.23  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB       perforation   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.85  Formula draft \u00b7 Cutaway   View in 3D  Download GLB       rollx_4   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.54  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB       rollx   \u03b8 = 130\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.70  Formula draft   View in 3D  Download GLB     Cylinder      capsule   \u03b8 = 150\u00b0 \u00b7 \u03c6 = 0.47  In package catalog \u00b7 Cutaway   View in 3D  Download GLB       3D model  Close       Download GLB    "}, {"title": "Triangular filament", "href": "triangle-example.html", "text": "Recover the angle from a synthetic density profile in a triangular pore.   Fit a triangular filament \n This example fits a synthetic  filament_w3c0  profile. The filament touches three walls and occupies zero corners. \n  Python    from  panda_md  import  TrianglePore, synthetic_profile\n\npore = TrianglePore(side_nm= 6 , length_nm= 12 , layer_width_nm= 6 )\nfilament = pore.interface( &quot;filament_w3c0&quot; )\ntruth = { &quot;theta&quot; :  150.0 ,  &quot;delta&quot; :  0.02 ,  &quot;phi&quot; :  0.5 }\nprofile = synthetic_profile(\n    filament, truth, density_bulk_per_nm3= 30 , noise_std= 0.005 , seed= 0 \n)\nresult = filament.fit(profile, density_bulk_per_nm3= 30 )\n print ( f&quot;Input theta = {truth[&#x27;theta&#x27;]:.2f} deg&quot; )\n print ( f&quot;Fit theta = {result.values[&#x27;theta&#x27;]:.2f} deg&quot; )\n print ( f&quot;Flags: {result.problems()}&quot; )     Output   Input theta = 150.00 deg\nFit theta = 149.83 deg\nFlags: ()    With the  plot  extra, draw the fitted curve over the synthetic data.   Python    import  matplotlib.pyplot  as  plt\n from  panda_md.plotting  import  plot_fit\n\nax = plot_fit(result)\nax.set_xlabel( &quot;Reduced coordinate, z/a&quot; )\nax.figure.savefig( &quot;triangle-fit.png&quot; , dpi= 150 )\nplt.show()      Archived synthetic fit for a triangular pore.  Download CSV  \u00b7  Download PNG .   "}, {"title": "From a trajectory", "href": "trajectories.html", "text": "Read a GROMACS or LAMMPS trajectory, inspect the contact angle across the full run, and fit a selected averaging window.   Download and run the examples \n Extract  md-trajectory-examples.zip  and  install PANDA with the  md  and  plot  extras . Run these commands from the extracted directory. Both examples use the same 201 independently generated particle frames, spanning 0\u201310 ns at 50 ps intervals. The input angle is 120\u00b0. The time axis exercises the trajectory workflow on synthetic coordinates. \n  Shell   python md_gromacs.py\npython md_lammps.py    Each script writes an NPZ with the full-run block profiles, an NPZ with the averaged profile, and a PNG with three diagnostic panels.    Choose an example \n \n  GROMACS  \u00b7 GRO topology, XTC trajectory, and residue selections. \n  LAMMPS  \u00b7 DATA topology, custom dump, atom types, and timestep. \n  Full trajectory and averaging window  \u00b7 profile, density map, and angle history. \n  Fit saved blocks  \u00b7 reuse existing density profiles. \n  "}, {"title": "GROMACS", "href": "trajectory-gromacs.html", "text": "Read a GRO or TPR topology and an XTC trajectory.   Run the GROMACS example \n  Download the example files and install the extras . \n The example reads  slit.gro  and  slit.xtc . For a simulation, use a matching  .tpr  or  .gro  with your trajectory, and substitute the residue and atom names from that topology. The XTC stores frame times. If counting water oxygens, use the bulk  oxygen number density  in nm\u207b\u00b3. \n  Python    from  panda_md  import  load_trajectory\n\n from  md_workflow  import  analyze\n\n\ntraj = load_trajectory( &quot;slit.gro&quot; ,  &quot;slit.xtc&quot; )\nanalyze(\n    traj,\n    walls= &quot;resname WALL&quot; ,\n    liquid= &quot;resname LIQ and name O&quot; ,\n    rho_bulk= 3.0 ,\n    average_from= &quot;2 ns&quot; ,\n    average_to= &quot;10 ns&quot; ,\n    block= &quot;0.5 ns&quot; ,\n    prefix= &quot;gromacs&quot; ,\n)     Output   Pore width = 8.000 nm\nTrajectory = 0 to 10000 ps\nAveraging window = 2000 to 10000 ps\nBlocks plotted = 20\nFull blocks inside averaging window = 16\nMean-profile theta = 120.40 deg\nBlock SD inside window = 2.50 deg\nFit flags = ()     Read the diagnostic figure  \u00b7  GROMACS file formats  \u00b7  MDAnalysis input and topology options   "}, {"title": "LAMMPS", "href": "trajectory-lammps.html", "text": "Read a DATA topology and a custom trajectory dump.   Run the LAMMPS example \n  Download the example files and install the extras . \n The example pairs an  atom_style atomic  DATA file with a custom dump. Type 1 is the wall and type 2 is the selected liquid. For your run, substitute its atom types and set  atom_style  to the columns in the DATA file\u2019s  Atoms  section. The dump and DATA file must have matching atom IDs. \n  Python    from  panda_md  import  load_trajectory\n\n from  md_workflow  import  analyze\n\n\ntraj = load_trajectory(\n     &quot;slit.data&quot; ,  &quot;slit.lammpstrj&quot; ,\n    atom_style= &quot;id type x y z&quot; ,\n    dt= 0.002 ,   # ps per integration step; dump interval is 25000 steps \n)\nanalyze(\n    traj,\n    walls= &quot;type 1&quot; ,\n    liquid= &quot;type 2&quot; ,\n    rho_bulk= 3.0 ,\n    average_from= &quot;2 ns&quot; ,\n    average_to= &quot;10 ns&quot; ,\n    block= &quot;0.5 ns&quot; ,\n    prefix= &quot;lammps&quot; ,\n)     Output   Pore width = 8.000 nm\nTrajectory = 0 to 10000 ps\nAveraging window = 2000 to 10000 ps\nBlocks plotted = 20\nFull blocks inside averaging window = 16\nMean-profile theta = 120.40 deg\nBlock SD inside window = 2.49 deg\nFit flags = ()      Write a compatible dump \n Use the integration timestep in  ps per step  for Python\u2019s  dt . Here, 25,000 steps \u00d7 0.002 ps gives 50 ps between saved frames. With  units real , convert the input timestep from fs to ps. With  units lj , convert reduced distances and times consistently before using physical nm and ps labels. PANDA's MDAnalysis reader converts input \u00c5 to nm. \n  Shell   write_data slit.data\ndump trajectory all custom 25000 slit.lammpstrj id type x y z\ndump_modify trajectory sort id     Read the diagnostic figure  \u00b7  LAMMPS dump command  \u00b7  LAMMPS units   "}, {"title": "Trajectory averaging", "href": "trajectory-averaging.html", "text": "Use the full angle history to show which frames contribute to the reported fit.   Full trajectory and averaging window \n Panel (a) shows the density map centered on the roll axis and the slit midplane. Panel (b) shows the density profile and its fit, with the slit midplane at  z/H  = 0. Both panels use the same 2\u201310 ns averaging window. \n Panel (c) shows all twenty 0.5 ns blocks across 0\u201310 ns. Open markers show the four early blocks. Green shading begins at 2 ns, and the horizontal dashed line gives the angle from fitting the averaged profile. \n   GROMACS-format example.  Download PNG .  \n Each block marker is placed at the midpoint of its sampled frames. PANDA drops an incomplete final block. The reported standard deviation uses the complete plotted blocks whose sampled frames lie within the averaging window. For production data, inspect equilibration before choosing the averaging start and account for temporal correlation when choosing the block length. \n   Shared Python workflow   Show the analysis and plotting code   Python    &quot;&quot;&quot;Analyze a slit-pore roll from a GROMACS or LAMMPS trajectory.&quot;&quot;&quot; \n\n from  pathlib  import  Path\n\n import  matplotlib.pyplot  as  plt\n import  numpy  as  np\n from  matplotlib.colors  import  LinearSegmentedColormap\n\n from  panda_md  import  SlitPore, density_map, density_profile, fit_blocks\n from  panda_md.core.timing  import  to_picoseconds\n\n\nSTYLE = Path(__file__).with_name( &quot;scientific.mplstyle&quot; )\nGREEN =  &quot;#276647&quot; \nMAP_COLORS = LinearSegmentedColormap.from_list(\n     &quot;pore_density&quot; , [ &quot;#fcfdfb&quot; ,  &quot;#e6f0e2&quot; ,  &quot;#a5c8a8&quot; ,  &quot;#589467&quot; ,  &quot;#245a3a&quot; ]\n)\n\n\n def  plot_diagnostics(density, result, width, rho_bulk, times, window, midpoint, angles, included, target):\n     with  plt.style.context(STYLE):\n        fig = plt.figure(figsize=( 6.4 ,  8.4 ))\n        map_ax = fig.add_axes([ 0.14 ,  0.61 ,  0.80 ,  0.80  *  6.4  *  0.55  /  8.4 ])\n        profile_ax = fig.add_axes([ 0.14 ,  0.35 ,  0.80 ,  0.185 ])\n        block_ax = fig.add_axes([ 0.14 ,  0.09 ,  0.80 ,  0.185 ])\n         for  index, ax  in   enumerate ((map_ax, profile_ax, block_ax)):\n            ax.text( 0 ,  1.025 ,  f&quot;({chr(97 + index)})&quot; , transform=ax.transAxes, va= &quot;bottom&quot; )\n\n        mesh = map_ax.pcolormesh(\n            density.length_edges_nm / width, density.height_edges_nm / width,\n            density.density_per_nm3.T / rho_bulk, shading= &quot;flat&quot; , cmap=MAP_COLORS, vmin= 0 ,\n        )\n         for  lower, upper  in  ((- 0.55 , - 0.5 ), ( 0.5 ,  0.55 )):\n            map_ax.axhspan(lower, upper, color= &quot;#d6d9d4&quot; , linewidth= 0 )\n        map_ax. set (xlim=(- 1 ,  1 ), ylim=(- 0.55 ,  0.55 ), xlabel= &quot;$x/H$&quot; , ylabel= &quot;$z/H$&quot; ,\n                   xticks=np.linspace(- 1 ,  1 ,  5 ), yticks=(- 0.5 ,  0 ,  0.5 ))\n        map_ax.set_aspect( &quot;equal&quot; )\n        color_ax = map_ax.inset_axes([ 0.06 ,  0.20 ,  0.022 ,  0.55 ])\n        colorbar = fig.colorbar(mesh, cax=color_ax, ticks=( 0 ,  0.5 ,  1 ))\n        colorbar.ax.tick_params(labelsize= 8 , length= 2 )\n        colorbar.ax.text(- 0.25 ,  1.06 ,  r&quot;$\\rho/\\rho_\\mathrm{bulk}$&quot; ,\n                         transform=colorbar.ax.transAxes, fontsize= 8 )\n\n        profile_ax.axvline( 0 , color= &quot;#b9c2b8&quot; , linestyle= &quot;:&quot; , linewidth= 0.8 )\n        profile_ax.plot(result.coordinate, result.data,  &quot;o&quot; , ms= 3 , mfc= &quot;white&quot; ,\n                        mec= &quot;#5f766a&quot; , mew= 0.8 , label= &quot;Sampled profile&quot; )\n        profile_ax.plot(result.coordinate, result.model_curve, color=GREEN, label= &quot;PANDA fit&quot; )\n        profile_ax. set (xlim=(- 0.5 ,  0.5 ), xlabel= &quot;$z/H$&quot; , ylabel= r&quot;$\\rho/\\rho_\\mathrm{bulk}$&quot; ,\n                       xticks=np.linspace(- 0.5 ,  0.5 ,  5 ))\n        profile_ax.legend(loc= &quot;lower center&quot; , ncol= 2 )\n\n        start, end = window /  1000 \n        midpoint_ns = midpoint /  1000 \n        block_ax.axvspan(start, end, color= &quot;#e7f0df&quot; , label= f&quot;Average: {start:g}\u2013{end:g} ns&quot; )\n        block_ax.axvline(start, color=GREEN, linestyle= &quot;:&quot; , linewidth= 1 )\n        block_ax.plot(midpoint_ns, angles, color= &quot;#a4aca5&quot; , linewidth= 0.9 )\n        block_ax.plot(midpoint_ns[~included], angles[~included],  &quot;o&quot; , ms= 4 , mfc= &quot;white&quot; , mec= &quot;#687870&quot; )\n        block_ax.plot(midpoint_ns[included], angles[included],  &quot;o&quot; , ms= 4 , color=GREEN)\n        block_ax.axhline(result.values[ &quot;theta&quot; ], color= &quot;#a45d2b&quot; , linestyle= &quot;--&quot; ,\n                         linewidth= 1.1 , label= &quot;Fit of averaged profile&quot; )\n        block_ax. set (xlim=np.asarray(times) /  1000 , xlabel= &quot;Time (ns)&quot; , ylabel= r&quot;$\\theta$ (deg)&quot; )\n        block_ax.margins(y= 0.22 )\n        block_ax.legend(loc= &quot;upper right&quot; , ncol= 2 )\n        fig.savefig(target, dpi= 200 )\n        plt.close(fig)\n\n\n def  analyze(traj, *, walls, liquid, rho_bulk, average_from, average_to, block, prefix):\n    prefix = Path(prefix)\n    times = traj.times_ps()\n    first_ps, last_ps =  float (times[ 0 ]),  float (times[- 1 ])\n    average_start = to_picoseconds(average_from)\n    average_end = to_picoseconds(average_to)\n     if   not  first_ps &lt;= average_start &lt; average_end &lt;= last_ps:\n         raise   ValueError ( &quot;The averaging window must lie within the trajectory.&quot; )\n    pore = SlitPore.from_trajectory(traj, walls=walls, liquid=liquid, time=average_from)\n    profiles = density_profile(\n        traj, pore, liquid, start=first_ps, block=block,\n        bins= 80 , centering= &quot;pore&quot; ,\n    )\n    average_profile = density_profile(\n        traj, pore, liquid, start=average_from, stop=average_to,\n        bins= 80 , centering= &quot;pore&quot; ,\n    ).mean()\n    roll = pore.interface( &quot;roll&quot; )\n    result = roll.fit(average_profile, density_bulk_per_nm3=rho_bulk)\n    blocks = fit_blocks(roll, profiles, result.spec)\n    midpoint = (blocks.block_start_ps + blocks.block_stop_ps) /  2 \n    angles = blocks.values( &quot;theta&quot; )\n    included = (blocks.block_start_ps &gt;= average_start) &amp; (blocks.block_stop_ps &lt;= average_end)\n\n     print ( f&quot;Pore width = {pore.width_nm:.3f} nm&quot; )\n     print ( f&quot;Trajectory = {first_ps:g} to {last_ps:g} ps&quot; )\n     print ( f&quot;Averaging window = {average_start:g} to {average_end:g} ps&quot; )\n     print ( f&quot;Blocks plotted = {len(angles)}&quot; )\n     print ( f&quot;Full blocks inside averaging window = {np.count_nonzero(included)}&quot; )\n     print ( f&quot;Mean-profile theta = {result.values[&#x27;theta&#x27;]:.2f} deg&quot; )\n     if  np.count_nonzero(included) &gt;=  2 :\n         print ( f&quot;Block SD inside window = {np.std(angles[included], ddof=1):.2f} deg&quot; )\n     print ( f&quot;Fit flags = {result.problems()}&quot; )\n\n    profiles.save(prefix.with_name(prefix.name +  &quot;-blocks.npz&quot; ))\n    average_profile.save(prefix.with_name(prefix.name +  &quot;-average.npz&quot; ))\n    density = density_map(\n        traj, pore, liquid, shape= &quot;roll&quot; , start=average_from, stop=average_to, bins=( 65 ,  40 ),\n    )\n    plot_diagnostics(\n        density, result, pore.width_nm, rho_bulk, (first_ps, last_ps),\n        np.array([average_start, average_end]), midpoint, angles, included,\n        prefix.with_name(prefix.name +  &quot;-diagnostics.png&quot; ),\n    )       Check the profile \n Match the bulk density to the selected particle representation. Check wall selections, centering, bin width, and the periodic box geometry. Reload the full-run profiles with  ProfileSet.load(\"gromacs-blocks.npz\")  and the averaged profile with  DensityProfile.load(\"gromacs-average.npz\") . Use the corresponding  lammps-  filenames for that run.  "}, {"title": "Fit saved blocks", "href": "block-example.html", "text": "Estimate the spread in contact angle from a saved set of density profiles.   Run the block analysis on example data \n Download  synthetic-roll-blocks.npz  into the working directory. The file contains eight independent synthetic profiles generated with a 120\u00b0 contact angle. \n  Python    from  panda_md  import  ProfileSet, SlitPore, fit_blocks\n\nprofiles = ProfileSet.load( &quot;synthetic-roll-blocks.npz&quot; )\npore = SlitPore(width_nm= 8.0 , length_nm= 16.0 )\nroll = pore.interface( &quot;roll&quot; )\nresult = roll.fit(profiles.mean(), density_bulk_per_nm3= 30.0 )\nblocks = fit_blocks(roll, profiles, result.spec)\n print (result.summary())\n print ( f&quot;Block SD = {blocks.std(&#x27;theta&#x27;):.3f} deg&quot; )\n print ( f&quot;Block mean = {blocks.mean(&#x27;theta&#x27;):.3f} deg&quot; )     Output   slit/roll  regime: non_wetting  loss: 0.0008747\n   theta = 119.985  (free)\n   delta = 0.0301568  (free)\n     phi = 0.400031  (fixed)\n   shift = 0  (fixed)\nBlock SD = 0.273 deg\nBlock mean = 119.992 deg     Python    import  matplotlib.pyplot  as  plt\n\nangles = blocks.values( &quot;theta&quot; )\nfig, ax = plt.subplots()\nax.plot( range ( 1 ,  len (angles) +  1 ), angles,  &quot;o&quot; , label= &quot;Block fit&quot; )\nax.axhline( 120 , linestyle= &quot;--&quot; , label= &quot;Input angle&quot; )\nax. set (xlabel= &quot;Synthetic block&quot; , ylabel= &quot;Contact angle (deg)&quot; )\nax.legend()\nplt.show()      Each marker is a separate fit. The dashed line marks the 120\u00b0 input.  Download the block angles .   "}, {"title": "Fitting and interpretation", "href": "fitting.html", "text": "Fit a candidate interface, inspect its diagnostics, and compare models in the physically accessible domain.   Fit a saved profile \n Download  density.csv  into the working directory. It contains the synthetic slit-pore profile from the quick start in physical units. A headerless input file contains coordinate in nm, number density in nm\u207b\u00b3, and an optional uncertainty column. Center the coordinates consistently with the analytical pore. \n  Python    from  panda_md  import  DensityProfile, SlitPore\n\nprofile = DensityProfile.load( &quot;density.csv&quot; )\npore = SlitPore(width_nm= 8.0 , length_nm= 16.0 )\nresult = pore.interface( &quot;roll&quot; ).fit(\n    profile, optimize=[ &quot;theta&quot; ,  &quot;delta&quot; ], density_bulk_per_nm3= 30.0 ,\n)\n print (result.summary())\n print (result.problems())     Output   slit/roll  regime: non_wetting  loss: 0.003774\n   theta = 120.614  (free)\n   delta = 0.0300547  (free)\n     phi = 0.40016  (fixed)\n   shift = 0  (fixed)\n()    An empty tuple  ()  means PANDA reported no diagnostic flags for this fit.    Parameters and normalization \n  theta  is the contact angle in degrees for the analyzed phase.  delta  is the effective wall-layer thickness as a fraction of the characteristic pore size.  phi  is the analyzed liquid\u2019s volume fraction.  shift  is an offset along the profile coordinate in pore-size units, fixed at zero by default. \n With bulk normalization, PANDA divides the input density by \u03c1 bulk  and can estimate \u03c6 from the profile. With mean normalization, supply the profile\u2019s particle count and pore volume, and fix or optimize \u03c6 if the bulk density is unavailable. \n   Fit diagnostics \n The default L1 objective is the mean absolute deviation of the normalized profiles. PANDA runs Nelder\u2013Mead from multiple starting points. Inspect convergence, feasibility, parameter bounds, and the  at_regime_boundary  flag. A boundary fit near 90\u00b0 may indicate that the selected model\u2019s angular range is too restrictive. \n  How noise and angle affect recovery  \n   Compare shapes and stability \n  compare_shapes(pore, profile, spec)  ranks available profiles by fit loss. Near-ties can occur when different interfaces project to nearly the same one-dimensional density. Inspect the density map or snapshots before assigning a morphology. \n  stability_diagram(...)  ranks feasible shapes by the capillary surface term S LV  \u2212 cos \u03b8 S SL  at prescribed angle and layer thickness. Each operation has its own set of supported shapes in the  catalog .  "}, {"title": "Angle recovery", "href": "validation.html", "text": "Compare the mean and maximum absolute errors on synthetic slit-pore rolls.   How noise and angle affect recovery \n The validation sweep used 200 bins and ten noise realizations at each setting. Panel (a) varies the noise at \u03b8 = 120\u00b0. Panel (b) varies the input angle at 0.5% noise. The maximum is the largest absolute error across the ten realizations. \n   Archived validation data.  Noise sweep CSV  \u00b7  Angle sweep CSV .   "}, {"title": "Command line", "href": "cli.html", "text": "Use panda to build profiles, fit a known shape, or compare candidate models from the shell.   Inspect available models   Shell   panda shapes --pore slit\npanda profile --help\npanda fit --help      Create a profile and fit it   Shell   panda profile system.tpr system.xtc --walls &quot;resname GRAPHITE&quot; --select &quot;resname WATER and name OW&quot; --start &quot;2 ns&quot; --block &quot;1 ns&quot; -o water.npz --pore-output pore.json\npanda fit water.npz --pore-file pore.json --shape roll --rho-bulk 33.1 --blocks -o result.json   \n Use  --shape auto  to compare supported candidates and  --plot fit.png  with the plotting extra. The exit codes are 0 for success, 1 for an input error, and 2 for a completed fit with diagnostic flags. \n   Save the workflow in TOML   TOML   [pore]\ntype = &quot;slit&quot;\nwall_selection = &quot;resname GRAPHITE&quot;\n\n[profile]\ntopology = &quot;system.tpr&quot;\ntrajectory = [&quot;system.xtc&quot;]\nselect = &quot;resname WATER and name OW&quot;\nstart = &quot;2 ns&quot;\nblock = &quot;1 ns&quot;\n\n[fit]\nshape = &quot;roll&quot;\ndensity_bulk_per_nm3 = 33.1\nblocks = true\noutput = &quot;result.json&quot;    Save as  panda.toml  and run  panda run panda.toml . Input paths are relative to the settings file.  "}, {"title": "Python API", "href": "api.html", "text": "Find functions, classes, parameters, and return types by topic.   Reference by topic      Topic  Description       Pores and models   Choose a geometry, discover its shapes, and evaluate an interface.     Fitting and results   Configure optimization, read parameters, and inspect diagnostic flags.     Profiles and trajectories   Load simulation files or arrays, then compute, store, or inspect densities.     Blocks and morphology   Compare fitted shapes, estimate block spread, and map capillary stability.     Synthetic data and accuracy   Generate known-angle test data and measure reconstruction error.     Plotting   Draw figures from existing PANDA objects. Requires the plot extra.     Enums and exceptions   Look up supported values and diagnose failures.        Version and imports  Signatures are generated from PANDA 0.1.0 alpha at commit   eff655e  . Most entries can be imported from  panda_md . Plotting helpers are in  panda_md.plotting . Definition links may require access to the package repository.  "}, {"title": "Citing PANDA", "href": "citation.html", "text": "Cite the original PANDA method and the studies relevant to your geometry or analysis.   Original method \n Semenchuk, Kondratyuk, and Kopanichuk introduced PANDA in  Colloids and Surfaces A , volume 708, article 135994. Include the package version or commit used in your methods. \n  BibTeX   @article{semenchuk2025panda,\n  author  = {Semenchuk, A. A. and Kondratyuk, N. D. and Kopanichuk, I. V.},\n  title   = {{PANDA}: Predicting angle from nanoscale density analysis},\n  journal = {Colloids and Surfaces A: Physicochemical and Engineering Aspects},\n  year    = {2025},\n  volume  = {708},\n  pages   = {135994},\n  doi     = {10.1016/j.colsurfa.2024.135994}\n}     Download BibTeX     Package paper  The manuscript describing the current software package is in preparation. Its citation will be added when it is available.    Related publications    The shape of the liquid-liquid interface for oil/water mixtures in slit pores  Kopanichuk et al. \u00b7 Colloids and Surfaces A 601 (2020), 124884    PANDA: Predicting angle from nanoscale density analysis  Semenchuk, Kondratyuk, and Kopanichuk \u00b7 Colloids and Surfaces A 708 (2025), 135994    Towards reproducible wetting studies: Automated contact angle determination by molecular simulations  Semenchuk et al. \u00b7 Colloids and Surfaces A 725 (2025), 137586    Characterisation of the dominant liquid-liquid interface shape in confined systems during molecular simulations  Shistko et al. \u00b7 Molecular Simulation 51(16) (2025), 1071\u20131080    From nanodroplets to macroscopic wettability for rough surfaces: Combining molecular simulations and experiments  Guskov et al. \u00b7 Journal of Molecular Liquids 439 (2025), 128861    The Effect of Adsorption Film Thickness on the Shape of the Interface Between Immiscible Liquids in a Flat Slitlike Pore  Semenchuk, Bakulin, Gerke, Kondratyuk, and Kopanichuk \u00b7 Colloid Journal 88(2) (2026), 211\u2013221    Assessing density equilibration in confined liquid\u2013liquid interfaces  Guskov et al. \u00b7 Molecular Simulation 52(7) (2026), 546\u2013555    The interface shape and contact angle determination for liquid-liquid systems in cylindrical nanopores  Vandyshev, Kondratyuk, Gerke, and Kopanichuk \u00b7 Capillarity 19(3) (2026), 86\u201396      Dynamic contact angles   PANDA-D: Interface-free determination of two dynamic contact angles  (preprint, 2026). The two-angle extension jointly analyzes density and layerwise center-of-mass displacement.  "}, {"title": "Pores and models", "href": "api-pores.html", "text": "Choose a geometry, discover its shapes, and evaluate an interface.   Pores and shapes guide \u2192    SlitPore   panda_md.SlitPore    SlitPore(\n    *,\n    normal_axis: core.enums.Axis = Axis.Z,\n    wall_selection: str | None = None,\n    width_nm: float,\n    length_nm: float,\n    base_aspect_ratio: float = 1.0,\n    length_axis: core.enums.Axis = Axis.X,\n    wall_offset_nm: float = 0.0,\n) -&gt; None   Parallel walls separated by width_nm. The characteristic size is the wall-to-wall gap.  Fields      Field  Type       normal_axis    core.enums.Axis      wall_selection    str | None      width_nm    float      length_nm    float      base_aspect_ratio    float      length_axis    core.enums.Axis      wall_offset_nm    float       Methods and properties    from_trajectory(\n    trajectory: core.trajectory.Trajectory,\n    *,\n    walls: str,\n    length_axis: core.enums.Axis = Axis.X,\n    normal_axis: core.enums.Axis = Axis.Z,\n    time: float | str = 0.0,\n    liquid: str | None = None,\n    wall_offset_nm: float = 0.0,\n) -&gt; SlitPore   Measure the wall-to-wall gap and box lengths from a selected trajectory frame.   shape_names() -&gt; tuple[str, ...]      interface(shape_name: str) -&gt; InterfaceModel      characteristic_size_nm() -&gt; float   Size to which the coordinate and \u03b4 are reduced: H for the slit, a for polygons.   volume_nm3() -&gt; float   Pore volume relative to which \u03c6 is defined.    View definition \u2197     TrianglePore   panda_md.TrianglePore    TrianglePore(\n    *,\n    normal_axis: core.enums.Axis = Axis.Z,\n    wall_selection: str | None = None,\n    side_nm: float,\n    length_nm: float,\n    layer_width_nm: float,\n) -&gt; None   Equilateral triangular channel. The characteristic size is side_nm.  Fields      Field  Type       normal_axis    core.enums.Axis      wall_selection    str | None      side_nm    float      length_nm    float      layer_width_nm    float       Methods and properties    shape_names() -&gt; tuple[str, ...]      interface(shape_name: str) -&gt; InterfaceModel      characteristic_size_nm() -&gt; float   Size to which the coordinate and \u03b4 are reduced: H for the slit, a for polygons.   volume_nm3() -&gt; float   Pore volume relative to which \u03c6 is defined.    View definition \u2197     SquarePore   panda_md.SquarePore    SquarePore(\n    *,\n    normal_axis: core.enums.Axis = Axis.Z,\n    wall_selection: str | None = None,\n    side_nm: float,\n    length_nm: float,\n    layer_width_nm: float,\n) -&gt; None   Square channel. The characteristic size is side_nm.  Fields      Field  Type       normal_axis    core.enums.Axis      wall_selection    str | None      side_nm    float      length_nm    float      layer_width_nm    float       Methods and properties    shape_names() -&gt; tuple[str, ...]      interface(shape_name: str) -&gt; InterfaceModel      characteristic_size_nm() -&gt; float   Size to which the coordinate and \u03b4 are reduced: H for the slit, a for polygons.   volume_nm3() -&gt; float   Pore volume relative to which \u03c6 is defined.    View definition \u2197     CylinderPore   panda_md.CylinderPore    CylinderPore(\n    *,\n    normal_axis: core.enums.Axis = Axis.Z,\n    wall_selection: str | None = None,\n    diameter_nm: float,\n    length_nm: float,\n    layer_width_nm: float,\n    axis: core.enums.Axis = Axis.X,\n    wall_offset_nm: float = 0.0,\n) -&gt; None   Circular channel. The characteristic size is diameter_nm.  Fields      Field  Type       normal_axis    core.enums.Axis      wall_selection    str | None      diameter_nm    float      length_nm    float      layer_width_nm    float      axis    core.enums.Axis      wall_offset_nm    float       Methods and properties    from_trajectory(\n    trajectory: core.trajectory.Trajectory,\n    *,\n    walls: str,\n    axis: core.enums.Axis | str = Axis.X,\n    normal_axis: core.enums.Axis | str = Axis.Z,\n    time: float | str = 0.0,\n    liquid: str | None = None,\n    wall_offset_nm: float = 0.0,\n) -&gt; CylinderPore   Measure the tube diameter and periodic length from the wall selection.   shape_names() -&gt; tuple[str, ...]      interface(shape_name: str) -&gt; InterfaceModel      characteristic_size_nm() -&gt; float   Size to which the coordinate and \u03b4 are reduced: H for the slit, a for polygons.   volume_nm3() -&gt; float   Pore volume relative to which \u03c6 is defined.    View definition \u2197     InterfaceModel   panda_md.InterfaceModel    InterfaceModel(pore: Pore, shape: InterfaceShape[Any]) -&gt; None   A named interface bound to a pore. Construct it with pore.interface(shape_name). Supply theta in degrees, delta and shift in reduced pore units, and phi as a fraction.  Methods and properties    default_optimize: tuple[str, ...]   The parameter names optimized by default for this shape.   profile(\n    coordinate: _typing._array_like._Buffer | _SupportsArray[dtype[Any]] | _NestedSequence[_SupportsArray[dtype[Any]]] | complex | bytes | str | _NestedSequence[complex | bytes | str],\n    **user_values: float,\n) -&gt; NDArray[float64]   Model \u03c1/\u03c1_bulk in the frame of reference of the shape formula.   is_feasible(**user_values: float) -&gt; bool   Whether the shape exists; outside the declared wetting regimes it does not.   phi_limits(**user_values: float) -&gt; tuple[float, float]   Lower and upper volume-fraction limits for the supplied parameters.   surface_terms(**user_values: float) -&gt; core.shape.SurfaceTerms   Return the interfacial areas used in the capillary-energy calculation.   capillary_energy(**user_values: float) -&gt; float   Compute the relative capillary energy from the model&#x27;s surface terms.   fit(\n    profile: core.profile.DensityProfile,\n    *,\n    optimize: Sequence[str] | None = None,\n    fixed: Mapping[str, float] | None = None,\n    bounds: Mapping[str, tuple[float, float]] | None = None,\n    initial: Mapping[str, float] | None = None,\n    normalization: core.enums.Normalization = Normalization.AUTO,\n    density_bulk_per_nm3: float | None = None,\n    loss: core.enums.LossFunction = LossFunction.L1,\n    window: tuple[float, float] | None = None,\n    starts_per_parameter: int = 5,\n    optimizer: core.enums.OptimizerMethod = OptimizerMethod.NELDER_MEAD,\n    regime: core.enums.Regime | None = None,\n) -&gt; FitResult   Fit this model to a density profile with the specified optimization settings.    View definition \u2197     Parameter   panda_md.Parameter    Parameter(\n    *,\n    name: str,\n    default: float | None,\n    bounds: tuple[float, float],\n    unit: core.enums.Unit = Unit.DIMENSIONLESS,\n    symbol: str = &#x27;&#x27;,\n    description: str = &#x27;&#x27;,\n    natural_lower_bound: bool = False,\n) -&gt; None   Definition of a shape parameter and its units, allowed range, and default value.  Fields      Field  Type       name    str      default    float | None      bounds    tuple[float, float]      unit    core.enums.Unit      symbol    str      description    str      natural_lower_bound    bool        View definition \u2197     SymmetryAxis   panda_md.SymmetryAxis    SymmetryAxis(*, orientation: core.enums.AxisOrientation, locate: core.enums.AxisLocator) -&gt; None   Orientation and location rule used to center a shape in trajectory maps.  Fields      Field  Type       orientation    core.enums.AxisOrientation      locate    core.enums.AxisLocator        View definition \u2197   "}, {"title": "Fitting and results", "href": "api-fitting.html", "text": "Configure optimization, read parameters, and inspect diagnostic flags.   Fitting guide \u2192    FitSpec   panda_md.FitSpec    FitSpec(\n    *,\n    optimize: tuple[str, ...] | None = None,\n    fixed: Mapping[str, float] = dict(),\n    bounds: Mapping[str, tuple[float, float]] = dict(),\n    initial: Mapping[str, float] = dict(),\n    normalization: core.enums.Normalization = Normalization.AUTO,\n    density_bulk_per_nm3: float | None = None,\n    loss: core.enums.LossFunction = LossFunction.L1,\n    window: tuple[float, float] | None = None,\n    starts_per_parameter: int = 5,\n    optimizer: core.enums.OptimizerMethod = OptimizerMethod.NELDER_MEAD,\n    regime: core.enums.Regime | None = None,\n) -&gt; None   Reusable settings for a fit, shape comparison, or block analysis. Bounds narrow the model domain. The fit window uses reduced coordinates.  Fields      Field  Type       optimize    tuple[str, ...] | None      fixed    Mapping[str, float]      bounds    Mapping[str, tuple[float, float]]      initial    Mapping[str, float]      normalization    core.enums.Normalization      density_bulk_per_nm3    float | None      loss    core.enums.LossFunction      window    tuple[float, float] | None      starts_per_parameter    int      optimizer    core.enums.OptimizerMethod      regime    core.enums.Regime | None        View definition \u2197     InterfaceModel.fit   panda_md.InterfaceModel.fit    fit(\n    profile: core.profile.DensityProfile,\n    *,\n    optimize: Sequence[str] | None = None,\n    fixed: Mapping[str, float] | None = None,\n    bounds: Mapping[str, tuple[float, float]] | None = None,\n    initial: Mapping[str, float] | None = None,\n    normalization: core.enums.Normalization = Normalization.AUTO,\n    density_bulk_per_nm3: float | None = None,\n    loss: core.enums.LossFunction = LossFunction.L1,\n    window: tuple[float, float] | None = None,\n    starts_per_parameter: int = 5,\n    optimizer: core.enums.OptimizerMethod = OptimizerMethod.NELDER_MEAD,\n    regime: core.enums.Regime | None = None,\n) -&gt; FitResult   Fit one DensityProfile and return a FitResult. Set density_bulk_per_nm3 for bulk normalization. The default loss is mean absolute deviation.  Parameters      Argument  Meaning       profile   DensityProfile in physical units.     optimize, fixed   Choose the free parameter names or assign fixed values. An omitted optimize uses the model defaults.     bounds, initial   Optionally narrow parameter bounds and supply an extra starting point in user units.     normalization, density_bulk_per_nm3   Auto normalization uses bulk density if supplied, otherwise the profile mean density.     window   Fit interval on the reduced profile coordinate.     regime   Restrict the search to a supported wetting regime.       View definition \u2197     FitResult   panda_md.FitResult    FitResult(\n    *,\n    pore_name: str,\n    shape_name: str,\n    regime: core.enums.Regime | None,\n    frame: core.enums.Frame,\n    normalization: core.enums.Normalization,\n    values: Mapping[str, float],\n    free_parameters: tuple[str, ...],\n    fixed_parameters: tuple[str, ...],\n    loss: float,\n    success: bool,\n    message: str,\n    start_count: int,\n    evaluation_count: int,\n    feasible: bool,\n    at_bounds: tuple[str, ...],\n    at_regime_boundary: bool,\n    wall_layer_thickness_nm: float | None,\n    density_bulk_derived_per_nm3: float | None,\n    volume_fraction_from_data: float | None,\n    coordinate: NDArray[float64],\n    data: NDArray[float64],\n    model_curve: NDArray[float64],\n    alternatives: tuple[core.result.FitResult, ...] = (),\n    spec: core.spec.FitSpec,\n    library_version: str | None = None,\n) -&gt; None   Fitted values, optimizer diagnostics, normalized fit data, and model curve. Use values[&#x27;theta&#x27;] for the contact angle when the shape has one.  Fields      Field  Type       pore_name    str      shape_name    str      regime    core.enums.Regime | None      frame    core.enums.Frame      normalization    core.enums.Normalization      values    Mapping[str, float]      free_parameters    tuple[str, ...]      fixed_parameters    tuple[str, ...]      loss    float      success    bool      message    str      start_count    int      evaluation_count    int      feasible    bool      at_bounds    tuple[str, ...]      at_regime_boundary    bool      wall_layer_thickness_nm    float | None      density_bulk_derived_per_nm3    float | None      volume_fraction_from_data    float | None      coordinate    NDArray[float64]      data    NDArray[float64]      model_curve    NDArray[float64]      alternatives    tuple[core.result.FitResult, ...]      spec    core.spec.FitSpec      library_version    str | None       Methods and properties    summary() -&gt; str   Return a human-readable summary of the result and its diagnostics.   problems() -&gt; tuple[str, ...]   Check flags: empty \u2014 the fit converged inside the existence domain and did not hit the bounds.    View definition \u2197   "}, {"title": "Profiles and trajectories", "href": "api-data.html", "text": "Load simulation files or arrays, then compute, store, or inspect densities.   Trajectory guide \u2192    load_trajectory   panda_md.load_trajectory    load_trajectory(\n    topology: str | pathlib.Path,\n    *trajectory_files: str | pathlib.Path,\n    **options: object,\n) -&gt; trajectory.reader.MDATrajectory   Open a topology and one or more trajectory files through MDAnalysis. Requires the md extra. Additional options go to MDAnalysis.Universe.   View definition \u2197     ArrayTrajectory   panda_md.ArrayTrajectory    ArrayTrajectory(\n    *,\n    positions_nm: NDArray[float64],\n    boxes_nm: NDArray[float64],\n    times_ps: NDArray[float64],\n    groups: Mapping[str, NDArray[int64]] = dict(),\n    molecule_ids: NDArray[int64] | None = None,\n    masses: NDArray[float64] | None = None,\n    axis_positions_nm: NDArray[float64] | None = None,\n) -&gt; None   In-memory trajectory. Supply particle positions and box lengths in nm, and frame times in ps.  Fields      Field  Type       positions_nm    NDArray[float64]      boxes_nm    NDArray[float64]      times_ps_values    NDArray[float64]      groups    Mapping[str, NDArray[int64]]      molecule_ids    NDArray[int64] | None      masses    NDArray[float64] | None      axis_positions_nm    NDArray[float64] | None       Methods and properties    select(selection: str | Sequence[int]) -&gt; NDArray[int64]   Atom indices of the selection. An empty selection \u2014 InvalidTrajectoryError.   times_ps() -&gt; NDArray[float64]   Time of each frame, ps.   frame_indices(\n    *,\n    start: float | str = 0.0,\n    stop: float | str | None = None,\n    stride: int = 1,\n) -&gt; list[int]      frames(\n    groups: Sequence[NDArray[int64]],\n    *,\n    start: float | str = 0.0,\n    stop: float | str | None = None,\n    stride: int = 1,\n) -&gt; Iterator[core.trajectory.TrajectoryFrame]   Frames with start \u2264 t \u2264 stop, every stride-th; streamed, without loading the whole trajectory into memory.    View definition \u2197     density_profile   panda_md.density_profile    density_profile(\n    trajectory: core.trajectory.Trajectory,\n    pore: core.pore.Pore,\n    select: str | Sequence[int],\n    *,\n    centering: core.enums.ProfileCentering | str | None = None,\n    bins: int = 200,\n    bin_width_nm: float | None = None,\n    start: float | str = 0.0,\n    stop: float | str | None = None,\n    block: float | str | None = None,\n    stride: int = 1,\n    pore_center_nm: float | None = None,\n    orientation: core.enums.Orientation | str = Orientation.AUTO,\n    per: core.enums.ParticleGrouping | str = ParticleGrouping.ATOM,\n) -&gt; core.profile.ProfileSet   Bin number density along the pore axis. The selection accepts an MDAnalysis selection string or atom indices. A numeric time is in ps. A block setting produces time-resolved profiles.  Parameters      Argument  Meaning       bins, bin_width_nm   Set the bin count or the width in nm.     start, stop, stride   Select a frame interval and subsample it. Time can be numeric ps or a string such as &#x27;2 ns&#x27;.     block   Length of a time block. The default returns a ProfileSet with one averaged profile.     centering, orientation   Choose the coordinate origin and whether PANDA may reflect the pore-frame profile.     per   Count atoms or molecule centers of mass.       View definition \u2197     DensityProfile   panda_md.DensityProfile    DensityProfile(\n    *,\n    coordinate_nm: NDArray[float64],\n    density_per_nm3: NDArray[float64],\n    density_sem_per_nm3: NDArray[float64] | None = None,\n    frame: core.enums.Frame = Frame.PORE,\n    particle_count: float | None = None,\n    pore_volume_nm3: float | None = None,\n    flipped: bool = False,\n    frame_count: int | None = None,\n) -&gt; None   One number-density profile with coordinates in nm and densities in nm\u207b\u00b3. Supports NPZ or CSV input and output.  Fields      Field  Type       coordinate_nm    NDArray[float64]      density_per_nm3    NDArray[float64]      density_sem_per_nm3    NDArray[float64] | None      frame    core.enums.Frame      particle_count    float | None      pore_volume_nm3    float | None      flipped    bool      frame_count    int | None       Methods and properties    load(path: str | pathlib.Path) -&gt; DensityProfile      save(path: str | pathlib.Path) -&gt; None   Save: .npz \u2014 everything; .csv \u2014 columns and metadata in comment lines.   mean_density_per_nm3() -&gt; float   n\u0304 = N / V \u2014 mean density of the liquid in the pore.    View definition \u2197     ProfileSet   panda_md.ProfileSet    ProfileSet(\n    *,\n    bin_edges_nm: NDArray[float64],\n    block_densities_per_nm3: NDArray[float64],\n    block_start_ps: NDArray[float64],\n    block_stop_ps: NDArray[float64],\n    block_frame_counts: tuple[int, ...],\n    block_particle_counts: NDArray[float64],\n    frame: core.enums.Frame,\n    centering: core.enums.ProfileCentering,\n    selection: str,\n    pore_volume_nm3: float | None = None,\n    flipped: bool = False,\n) -&gt; None   One or more profiles on a common bin grid. The time bounds and frame counts describe the samples contributing to each block. Use NPZ to persist the set.  Fields      Field  Type       bin_edges_nm    NDArray[float64]      block_densities_per_nm3    NDArray[float64]      block_start_ps    NDArray[float64]      block_stop_ps    NDArray[float64]      block_frame_counts    tuple[int, ...]      block_particle_counts    NDArray[float64]      frame    core.enums.Frame      centering    core.enums.ProfileCentering      selection    str      pore_volume_nm3    float | None      flipped    bool       Methods and properties    load(path: str | pathlib.Path) -&gt; ProfileSet      save(path: str | pathlib.Path) -&gt; None   Save to .npz (arrays and metadata).   mean() -&gt; core.profile.DensityProfile   Return the mean over blocks.   block(index: int) -&gt; core.profile.DensityProfile      std() -&gt; NDArray[float64]   Standard deviation of the density over blocks (0 for a single block).   sem() -&gt; NDArray[float64]   Standard error of the mean over blocks: std / \u221a(number of blocks).   block_count: int   Number of available profiles or time blocks.   coordinate_nm: NDArray[float64]   Common bin centers in nm.    View definition \u2197     density_map   panda_md.density_map    density_map(\n    trajectory: core.trajectory.Trajectory,\n    pore: pores.slit.pore.SlitPore,\n    select: str | Sequence[int],\n    *,\n    shape: str | None = None,\n    centering: core.enums.ProfileCentering | str | None = None,\n    bins: tuple[int, int] = (100, 100),\n    start: float | str = 0.0,\n    stop: float | str | None = None,\n    stride: int = 1,\n    pore_center_nm: float | None = None,\n    per: core.enums.ParticleGrouping | str = ParticleGrouping.ATOM,\n    orientation: core.enums.Orientation | str = Orientation.AUTO,\n    width_window_nm: float | None = None,\n) -&gt; trajectory.maps.DensityMap   Compute a two-dimensional number-density map in a slit pore. A supported shape name enables alignment on the shape symmetry axis.  Parameters      Argument  Meaning       bins   Number of bins along the long side and profile axis.     shape   Optional interface name for locating the in-plane symmetry axis.     width_window_nm   Optional strip width along the short side for a vertical symmetry axis.       View definition \u2197     DensityMap   panda_md.DensityMap    DensityMap(\n    *,\n    length_edges_nm: NDArray[float64],\n    height_edges_nm: NDArray[float64],\n    density_per_nm3: NDArray[float64],\n    frame: core.enums.Frame,\n    axis_centered: bool,\n    flipped: bool = False,\n    width_window_nm: float | None = None,\n    frame_count: int,\n    selection: str,\n) -&gt; None   Binned two-dimensional number density in nm\u207b\u00b3 and its bin edges in nm.  Fields      Field  Type       length_edges_nm    NDArray[float64]      height_edges_nm    NDArray[float64]      density_per_nm3    NDArray[float64]      frame    core.enums.Frame      axis_centered    bool      flipped    bool      width_window_nm    float | None      frame_count    int      selection    str        View definition \u2197   "}, {"title": "Blocks and morphology", "href": "api-analysis.html", "text": "Compare fitted shapes, estimate block spread, and map capillary stability.   Block averaging example \u2192    fit_blocks   panda_md.fit_blocks    fit_blocks(\n    model: core.model.InterfaceModel,\n    profiles: core.profile.ProfileSet,\n    spec: core.spec.FitSpec | None = None,\n) -&gt; analysis.blocks.FitResultSet   Fit each block of a ProfileSet with the same model and settings.   View definition \u2197     FitResultSet   panda_md.FitResultSet    FitResultSet(\n    *,\n    results: tuple[core.result.FitResult, ...],\n    block_start_ps: NDArray[float64],\n    block_stop_ps: NDArray[float64],\n) -&gt; None   Per-block fits and summary statistics. Interpret SEM as uncertainty of the mean only when blocks are sufficiently independent.  Fields      Field  Type       results    tuple[core.result.FitResult, ...]      block_start_ps    NDArray[float64]      block_stop_ps    NDArray[float64]       Methods and properties    values(name: str) -&gt; NDArray[float64]   Value of the parameter (user units) in each block.   mean(name: str) -&gt; float   Return the mean over blocks.   std(name: str) -&gt; float   Spread over blocks; not defined (nan) for a single block.   sem(name: str) -&gt; float   Standard error of the mean: std / \u221a(number of blocks) \u2014 valid if the blocks exceed the correlation time.   summary() -&gt; str   Return a human-readable summary of the result and its diagnostics.    View definition \u2197     statistical_inefficiency   panda_md.statistical_inefficiency    statistical_inefficiency(\n    values: Sequence[float] | NDArray[float64],\n    max_block_length: int | None = None,\n) -&gt; analysis.blocks.StatisticalInefficiency   Estimate how the variance of block means changes with block length for a series.   View definition \u2197     StatisticalInefficiency   panda_md.StatisticalInefficiency    StatisticalInefficiency(\n    *,\n    block_lengths: tuple[int, ...],\n    inefficiency: NDArray[float64],\n    series_length: int,\n) -&gt; None   Block lengths and estimated inefficiencies, with a plateau estimate when enough reliable lengths exist.  Fields      Field  Type       block_lengths    tuple[int, ...]      inefficiency    NDArray[float64]      series_length    int       Methods and properties    plateau() -&gt; float   Mean s over the last third of the lengths with at least MIN_BLOCKS blocks (otherwise over the last third    View definition \u2197     compare_shapes   panda_md.compare_shapes    compare_shapes(\n    pore: core.pore.Pore,\n    profile: core.profile.DensityProfile,\n    spec: core.spec.FitSpec | None = None,\n    shape_names: Sequence[str] | None = None,\n) -&gt; analysis.compare.ShapeComparison   Fit candidate shapes to the same profile and rank by loss. The result retains skipped shapes and records nearly indistinguishable candidates.  Parameters      Argument  Meaning       spec   Fit settings shared by the candidate shapes.     shape_names   Optional list of shapes to compare. By default, use all registered shapes for the pore.       View definition \u2197     ShapeComparison   panda_md.ShapeComparison    ShapeComparison(*, pore_name: str, rows: tuple[analysis.compare.ShapeFit, ...]) -&gt; None   Comparison of feasible fits and skipped candidates.  Fields      Field  Type       pore_name    str      rows    tuple[analysis.compare.ShapeFit, ...]       Methods and properties    fitted: tuple[core.result.FitResult, ...]   Successful candidate fits, in ranking order.   best: core.result.FitResult   The lowest-loss fitted candidate.   indistinguishable: tuple[str, ...]   Feasible shapes with a loss at most LOSS_TIE_FRACTION above the best: the profile cannot tell them apart.   summary() -&gt; str   Return a human-readable summary of the result and its diagnostics.    View definition \u2197     ShapeFit   panda_md.ShapeFit    ShapeFit(\n    *,\n    shape_name: str,\n    result: core.result.FitResult | None = None,\n    skipped_reason: str | None = None,\n) -&gt; None   One candidate&#x27;s fit result or the reason PANDA skipped it.  Fields      Field  Type       shape_name    str      result    core.result.FitResult | None      skipped_reason    str | None        View definition \u2197     stability_diagram   panda_md.stability_diagram    stability_diagram(\n    pore: core.pore.Pore,\n    *,\n    contact_angle_deg: float,\n    wall_layer: float,\n    volume_fractions: Sequence[float],\n    length_ratios: Sequence[float],\n    shape_names: Sequence[str] | None = None,\n) -&gt; analysis.stability.StabilityDiagram   Find the minimum capillary energy over volume fractions and reduced pore lengths at a fixed angle and wall-layer thickness.  Parameters      Argument  Meaning       contact_angle_deg, wall_layer   Fixed contact angle in degrees and effective wall-layer thickness in reduced pore units.     volume_fractions, length_ratios   Grid coordinates. Length ratios are relative to the characteristic pore size.     shape_names   Optional restriction to the listed morphologies.       View definition \u2197     StabilityDiagram   panda_md.StabilityDiagram    StabilityDiagram(\n    *,\n    pore_name: str,\n    contact_angle_deg: float,\n    wall_layer: float,\n    volume_fractions: tuple[float, ...],\n    length_ratios: tuple[float, ...],\n    shape_names: tuple[str, ...],\n    stable_shapes: tuple[tuple[str | None, ...], ...],\n) -&gt; None   Grid of stable shape names, indexed by length ratio then volume fraction. None means no candidate exists at that point.  Fields      Field  Type       pore_name    str      contact_angle_deg    float      wall_layer    float      volume_fractions    tuple[float, ...]      length_ratios    tuple[float, ...]      shape_names    tuple[str, ...]      stable_shapes    tuple[tuple[str | None, ...], ...]        View definition \u2197   "}, {"title": "Synthetic data and accuracy", "href": "api-synthetic.html", "text": "Generate known-angle test data and measure reconstruction error.   Angle recovery example \u2192    synthetic_profile   panda_md.synthetic_profile    synthetic_profile(\n    model: core.model.InterfaceModel,\n    values: Mapping[str, float],\n    *,\n    density_bulk_per_nm3: float,\n    bin_count: int = 200,\n    noise_std: float = 0.0,\n    frame: core.enums.Frame = Frame.PORE,\n    offset: float = 0.0,\n    seed: int | None = None,\n    noise_model: core.enums.NoiseModel = NoiseModel.CONSTANT,\n    sampling: core.enums.ProfileSampling = ProfileSampling.CENTER,\n) -&gt; core.profile.DensityProfile   Generate a one-dimensional profile for known model parameters. Set seed for repeatable noise.  Parameters      Argument  Meaning       values   Model parameters in user units, including theta in degrees where applicable.     noise_std, noise_model, seed   Noise magnitude relative to bulk density, its scaling rule, and the random seed.     sampling   Evaluate at bin centers or average within each bin.       View definition \u2197     synthetic_trajectory   panda_md.synthetic_trajectory    synthetic_trajectory(\n    model: core.model.InterfaceModel,\n    values: Mapping[str, float],\n    *,\n    density_bulk_per_nm3: float,\n    frame_count: int = 10,\n    time_step_ps: float = 10.0,\n    substrate_nm: float = 1.0,\n    seed: int | None = None,\n) -&gt; trajectory.arrays.ArrayTrajectory   Sample particle coordinates for a slit-pore shape that implements point containment. The returned trajectory includes liquid and walls groups.   View definition \u2197     AccuracyCase   panda_md.analysis.accuracy.AccuracyCase    AccuracyCase(\n    *,\n    truth: dict[str, float],\n    noise_std: float,\n    bin_count: int = 200,\n    offset: float = 0.0,\n    frame: core.enums.Frame = Frame.PORE,\n    optimize: tuple[str, ...] | None = None,\n    fixed: dict[str, float] = dict(),\n    noise_model: core.enums.NoiseModel = NoiseModel.POISSON,\n    sampling: core.enums.ProfileSampling = ProfileSampling.BIN_AVERAGE,\n) -&gt; None   Configuration for one synthetic recovery case, including the input parameters and noise settings.  Fields      Field  Type       truth    dict[str, float]      noise_std    float      bin_count    int      offset    float      frame    core.enums.Frame      optimize    tuple[str, ...] | None      fixed    dict[str, float]      noise_model    core.enums.NoiseModel      sampling    core.enums.ProfileSampling        View definition \u2197     angle_errors   panda_md.analysis.accuracy.angle_errors    angle_errors(\n    model: core.model.InterfaceModel,\n    case: analysis.accuracy.AccuracyCase,\n    *,\n    density_bulk_per_nm3: float,\n    seeds: Sequence[int],\n) -&gt; analysis.accuracy.AngleErrors   Repeat a synthetic fit with independent seeds and collect fitted-angle errors.   View definition \u2197     AngleErrors   panda_md.analysis.accuracy.AngleErrors    AngleErrors(*, errors_deg: NDArray[float64], at_bound: tuple[bool, ...]) -&gt; None   Per-seed errors in degrees (fitted minus input) and flags for fits at the angle bound.  Fields      Field  Type       errors_deg    NDArray[float64]      at_bound    tuple[bool, ...]        View definition \u2197     accuracy_study   panda_md.analysis.accuracy.accuracy_study    accuracy_study(\n    model: core.model.InterfaceModel,\n    varied: str,\n    cases: Mapping[str, tuple[float, analysis.accuracy.AccuracyCase]],\n    *,\n    density_bulk_per_nm3: float,\n    seeds: Sequence[int],\n) -&gt; analysis.accuracy.AccuracyStudy   Run a collection of synthetic recovery cases.   View definition \u2197     AccuracyStudy   panda_md.analysis.accuracy.AccuracyStudy    AccuracyStudy(\n    *,\n    shape_name: str,\n    varied: str,\n    labels: tuple[str, ...],\n    values: NDArray[float64],\n    errors_deg: NDArray[float64],\n    at_bound_counts: tuple[int, ...],\n) -&gt; None   Collect case-by-case angle errors for tables or figures.  Fields      Field  Type       shape_name    str      varied    str      labels    tuple[str, ...]      values    NDArray[float64]      errors_deg    NDArray[float64]      at_bound_counts    tuple[int, ...]       Methods and properties    mean_absolute() -&gt; NDArray[float64]      maximum_absolute() -&gt; NDArray[float64]      bias() -&gt; NDArray[float64]   Systematic shift: the mean of (recovered \u2212 true).   table() -&gt; str   Format the accuracy metrics as a text table.    View definition \u2197     NoiseModel   panda_md.core.enums.NoiseModel   Noise model for a synthetic density profile.      Member  Value       CONSTANT    constant      POISSON    poisson        View definition \u2197     ProfileSampling   panda_md.core.enums.ProfileSampling   Use the center of each bin or average the model across the bin.      Member  Value       CENTER    center      BIN_AVERAGE    bin_average        View definition \u2197   "}, {"title": "Plotting", "href": "api-plotting.html", "text": "Draw figures from existing PANDA objects. Requires the plot extra.   Plot a fit and residuals \u2192    plot_profile   panda_md.plotting.plot_profile    plot_profile(\n    profile: core.profile.DensityProfile | core.profile.ProfileSet,\n    ax: axes._axes.Axes | None = None,\n) -&gt; axes._axes.Axes   Draw one density profile or a mean with block-based standard errors.   View definition \u2197     plot_fit   panda_md.plotting.plot_fit    plot_fit(result: core.result.FitResult, ax: axes._axes.Axes | None = None) -&gt; axes._axes.Axes   Overlay normalized data and the fitted curve on the fit coordinate.   View definition \u2197     plot_blocks   panda_md.plotting.plot_blocks    plot_blocks(\n    blocks: analysis.blocks.FitResultSet,\n    parameter: str = &#x27;theta&#x27;,\n    ax: axes._axes.Axes | None = None,\n) -&gt; axes._axes.Axes   Draw one fitted parameter at the midpoint of each time block.   View definition \u2197     plot_density_map   panda_md.plotting.plot_density_map    plot_density_map(\n    density: trajectory.maps.DensityMap,\n    ax: axes._axes.Axes | None = None,\n) -&gt; axes._axes.Axes   Render a slit-pore number-density map with a colorbar.   View definition \u2197     plot_stability   panda_md.plotting.plot_stability    plot_stability(\n    diagram: analysis.stability.StabilityDiagram,\n    ax: axes._axes.Axes | None = None,\n) -&gt; axes._axes.Axes   Render stable morphologies on the volume-fraction and reduced-length grid.   View definition \u2197     plot_accuracy   panda_md.plotting.plot_accuracy    plot_accuracy(\n    study: analysis.accuracy.AccuracyStudy,\n    ax: axes._axes.Axes | None = None,\n) -&gt; axes._axes.Axes   Visualize angle errors across synthetic recovery cases.   View definition \u2197     save_fit_figure   panda_md.plotting.save_fit_figure    save_fit_figure(result: core.result.FitResult, path: str | pathlib.Path, dpi: int = 150) -&gt; None   Export the fit figure to a file. Its extension determines the format.   View definition \u2197     supported_figure_formats   panda_md.plotting.supported_figure_formats    supported_figure_formats() -&gt; tuple[str, ...]   List formats supported by the Matplotlib writer.   View definition \u2197   "}, {"title": "Enums and exceptions", "href": "api-types.html", "text": "Look up supported values and diagnose failures.   Fit diagnostics guide \u2192    Axis   panda_md.Axis   Cartesian axis of the rectangular simulation box.      Member  Value       X    x      Y    y      Z    z       Methods and properties    column: int   Column index of the coordinate in the position array (x \u2014 0, y \u2014 1, z \u2014 2).    View definition \u2197     AxisLocator   panda_md.AxisLocator   Rule for locating the symmetry axis within a frame.      Member  Value       LIQUID_CENTER    liquid_center      VOID_CENTER    void_center        View definition \u2197     AxisOrientation   panda_md.AxisOrientation   Direction of a shape symmetry axis relative to the walls.      Member  Value       VERTICAL    vertical      HORIZONTAL    horizontal        View definition \u2197     Frame   panda_md.Frame   Coordinate frame in which the density profile is expressed.      Member  Value       PORE    pore      LIQUID    liquid        View definition \u2197     LossFunction   panda_md.LossFunction   Mean absolute or mean squared deviation between profiles.      Member  Value       L1    l1      L2    l2        View definition \u2197     Normalization   panda_md.Normalization   Choice of bulk or mean density normalization.      Member  Value       AUTO    auto      BULK    bulk      MEAN    mean        View definition \u2197     OptimizerMethod   panda_md.OptimizerMethod   Local optimizer used by the fit.      Member  Value       NELDER_MEAD    Nelder-Mead      POWELL    Powell      LBFGSB    L-BFGS-B        View definition \u2197     Orientation   panda_md.Orientation   Whether pore-frame profiles can be reflected along the normal axis.      Member  Value       AUTO    auto      KEEP    keep        View definition \u2197     ParameterName   panda_md.ParameterName   Standard keys in result values and fit settings.      Member  Value       CONTACT_ANGLE    theta      WALL_LAYER_THICKNESS    delta      VOLUME_FRACTION    phi      PROFILE_SHIFT    shift        View definition \u2197     ParticleGrouping   panda_md.ParticleGrouping   Count selected atoms or centers of mass of molecules.      Member  Value       ATOM    atom      MOLECULE    molecule        View definition \u2197     ProfileCentering   panda_md.ProfileCentering   Reference point placed at zero for each profile.      Member  Value       PORE    pore      LIQUID    liquid        View definition \u2197     Regime   panda_md.Regime   Wetting or non-wetting regime of the selected liquid.      Member  Value       WETTING    wetting      NON_WETTING    non_wetting        View definition \u2197     Unit   panda_md.Unit   Unit convention used for a model parameter.      Member  Value       DEGREE    degree      PORE_SIZE    pore_size      DIMENSIONLESS    dimensionless        View definition \u2197     PandaError   panda_md.PandaError   Base exception for errors reported by PANDA.   View definition \u2197     PandaWarning   panda_md.PandaWarning   Base warning emitted for diagnostic conditions.   View definition \u2197     InfeasibleParametersError   panda_md.InfeasibleParametersError   The parameters do not admit the requested morphology.   View definition \u2197     InvalidProfileError   panda_md.InvalidProfileError   The input density profile is invalid or lacks required metadata.   View definition \u2197     InvalidTrajectoryError   panda_md.InvalidTrajectoryError   The trajectory, frame selection, or box geometry is invalid for the requested operation.   View definition \u2197     MissingDependencyError   panda_md.MissingDependencyError   An optional package required by the requested operation is missing.   View definition \u2197     NotDerivedError   panda_md.NotDerivedError   The requested analytical operation has no implementation for this shape or pore.   View definition \u2197     ProfileMismatchError   panda_md.ProfileMismatchError   The input profile and model are incompatible.   View definition \u2197     UnsupportedRegimeError   panda_md.UnsupportedRegimeError   The requested wetting regime is unavailable for the model.   View definition \u2197     __version__   panda_md.__version__   Installed package version string.  "}, {"title": "SlitPore", "href": "api-pores.html#slitpore", "text": "panda_md.SlitPore Parallel walls separated by width_nm. The characteristic size is the wall-to-wall gap."}, {"title": "SlitPore.from_trajectory", "href": "api-pores.html#slitpore-from_trajectory", "text": "panda_md.SlitPore.from_trajectory Measure the wall-to-wall gap and box lengths from a selected trajectory frame."}, {"title": "SlitPore.shape_names", "href": "api-pores.html#slitpore-shape_names", "text": "panda_md.SlitPore.shape_names "}, {"title": "SlitPore.interface", "href": "api-pores.html#slitpore-interface", "text": "panda_md.SlitPore.interface "}, {"title": "SlitPore.characteristic_size_nm", "href": "api-pores.html#slitpore-characteristic_size_nm", "text": "panda_md.SlitPore.characteristic_size_nm Size to which the coordinate and \u03b4 are reduced: H for the slit, a for polygons."}, {"title": "SlitPore.volume_nm3", "href": "api-pores.html#slitpore-volume_nm3", "text": "panda_md.SlitPore.volume_nm3 Pore volume relative to which \u03c6 is defined."}, {"title": "TrianglePore", "href": "api-pores.html#trianglepore", "text": "panda_md.TrianglePore Equilateral triangular channel. The characteristic size is side_nm."}, {"title": "TrianglePore.shape_names", "href": "api-pores.html#trianglepore-shape_names", "text": "panda_md.TrianglePore.shape_names "}, {"title": "TrianglePore.interface", "href": "api-pores.html#trianglepore-interface", "text": "panda_md.TrianglePore.interface "}, {"title": "TrianglePore.characteristic_size_nm", "href": "api-pores.html#trianglepore-characteristic_size_nm", "text": "panda_md.TrianglePore.characteristic_size_nm Size to which the coordinate and \u03b4 are reduced: H for the slit, a for polygons."}, {"title": "TrianglePore.volume_nm3", "href": "api-pores.html#trianglepore-volume_nm3", "text": "panda_md.TrianglePore.volume_nm3 Pore volume relative to which \u03c6 is defined."}, {"title": "SquarePore", "href": "api-pores.html#squarepore", "text": "panda_md.SquarePore Square channel. The characteristic size is side_nm."}, {"title": "SquarePore.shape_names", "href": "api-pores.html#squarepore-shape_names", "text": "panda_md.SquarePore.shape_names "}, {"title": "SquarePore.interface", "href": "api-pores.html#squarepore-interface", "text": "panda_md.SquarePore.interface "}, {"title": "SquarePore.characteristic_size_nm", "href": "api-pores.html#squarepore-characteristic_size_nm", "text": "panda_md.SquarePore.characteristic_size_nm Size to which the coordinate and \u03b4 are reduced: H for the slit, a for polygons."}, {"title": "SquarePore.volume_nm3", "href": "api-pores.html#squarepore-volume_nm3", "text": "panda_md.SquarePore.volume_nm3 Pore volume relative to which \u03c6 is defined."}, {"title": "CylinderPore", "href": "api-pores.html#cylinderpore", "text": "panda_md.CylinderPore Circular channel. The characteristic size is diameter_nm."}, {"title": "CylinderPore.from_trajectory", "href": "api-pores.html#cylinderpore-from_trajectory", "text": "panda_md.CylinderPore.from_trajectory Measure the tube diameter and periodic length from the wall selection."}, {"title": "CylinderPore.shape_names", "href": "api-pores.html#cylinderpore-shape_names", "text": "panda_md.CylinderPore.shape_names "}, {"title": "CylinderPore.interface", "href": "api-pores.html#cylinderpore-interface", "text": "panda_md.CylinderPore.interface "}, {"title": "CylinderPore.characteristic_size_nm", "href": "api-pores.html#cylinderpore-characteristic_size_nm", "text": "panda_md.CylinderPore.characteristic_size_nm Size to which the coordinate and \u03b4 are reduced: H for the slit, a for polygons."}, {"title": "CylinderPore.volume_nm3", "href": "api-pores.html#cylinderpore-volume_nm3", "text": "panda_md.CylinderPore.volume_nm3 Pore volume relative to which \u03c6 is defined."}, {"title": "InterfaceModel", "href": "api-pores.html#interfacemodel", "text": "panda_md.InterfaceModel A named interface bound to a pore. Construct it with pore.interface(shape_name). Supply theta in degrees, delta and shift in reduced pore units, and phi as a fraction."}, {"title": "InterfaceModel.default_optimize", "href": "api-pores.html#interfacemodel-default_optimize", "text": "panda_md.InterfaceModel.default_optimize The parameter names optimized by default for this shape."}, {"title": "InterfaceModel.profile", "href": "api-pores.html#interfacemodel-profile", "text": "panda_md.InterfaceModel.profile Model \u03c1/\u03c1_bulk in the frame of reference of the shape formula."}, {"title": "InterfaceModel.is_feasible", "href": "api-pores.html#interfacemodel-is_feasible", "text": "panda_md.InterfaceModel.is_feasible Whether the shape exists; outside the declared wetting regimes it does not."}, {"title": "InterfaceModel.phi_limits", "href": "api-pores.html#interfacemodel-phi_limits", "text": "panda_md.InterfaceModel.phi_limits Lower and upper volume-fraction limits for the supplied parameters."}, {"title": "InterfaceModel.surface_terms", "href": "api-pores.html#interfacemodel-surface_terms", "text": "panda_md.InterfaceModel.surface_terms Return the interfacial areas used in the capillary-energy calculation."}, {"title": "InterfaceModel.capillary_energy", "href": "api-pores.html#interfacemodel-capillary_energy", "text": "panda_md.InterfaceModel.capillary_energy Compute the relative capillary energy from the model's surface terms."}, {"title": "Parameter", "href": "api-pores.html#parameter", "text": "panda_md.Parameter Definition of a shape parameter and its units, allowed range, and default value."}, {"title": "SymmetryAxis", "href": "api-pores.html#symmetryaxis", "text": "panda_md.SymmetryAxis Orientation and location rule used to center a shape in trajectory maps."}, {"title": "FitSpec", "href": "api-fitting.html#fitspec", "text": "panda_md.FitSpec Reusable settings for a fit, shape comparison, or block analysis. Bounds narrow the model domain. The fit window uses reduced coordinates."}, {"title": "InterfaceModel.fit", "href": "api-fitting.html#interfacemodel-fit", "text": "panda_md.InterfaceModel.fit Fit one DensityProfile and return a FitResult. Set density_bulk_per_nm3 for bulk normalization. The default loss is mean absolute deviation."}, {"title": "FitResult", "href": "api-fitting.html#fitresult", "text": "panda_md.FitResult Fitted values, optimizer diagnostics, normalized fit data, and model curve. Use values['theta'] for the contact angle when the shape has one."}, {"title": "FitResult.summary", "href": "api-fitting.html#fitresult-summary", "text": "panda_md.FitResult.summary Return a human-readable summary of the result and its diagnostics."}, {"title": "FitResult.problems", "href": "api-fitting.html#fitresult-problems", "text": "panda_md.FitResult.problems Check flags: empty \u2014 the fit converged inside the existence domain and did not hit the bounds."}, {"title": "load_trajectory", "href": "api-data.html#load_trajectory", "text": "panda_md.load_trajectory Open a topology and one or more trajectory files through MDAnalysis. Requires the md extra. Additional options go to MDAnalysis.Universe."}, {"title": "ArrayTrajectory", "href": "api-data.html#arraytrajectory", "text": "panda_md.ArrayTrajectory In-memory trajectory. Supply particle positions and box lengths in nm, and frame times in ps."}, {"title": "ArrayTrajectory.select", "href": "api-data.html#arraytrajectory-select", "text": "panda_md.ArrayTrajectory.select Atom indices of the selection. An empty selection \u2014 InvalidTrajectoryError."}, {"title": "ArrayTrajectory.times_ps", "href": "api-data.html#arraytrajectory-times_ps", "text": "panda_md.ArrayTrajectory.times_ps Time of each frame, ps."}, {"title": "ArrayTrajectory.frame_indices", "href": "api-data.html#arraytrajectory-frame_indices", "text": "panda_md.ArrayTrajectory.frame_indices "}, {"title": "ArrayTrajectory.frames", "href": "api-data.html#arraytrajectory-frames", "text": "panda_md.ArrayTrajectory.frames Frames with start \u2264 t \u2264 stop, every stride-th; streamed, without loading the whole trajectory into memory."}, {"title": "density_profile", "href": "api-data.html#density_profile", "text": "panda_md.density_profile Bin number density along the pore axis. The selection accepts an MDAnalysis selection string or atom indices. A numeric time is in ps. A block setting produces time-resolved profiles."}, {"title": "DensityProfile", "href": "api-data.html#densityprofile", "text": "panda_md.DensityProfile One number-density profile with coordinates in nm and densities in nm\u207b\u00b3. Supports NPZ or CSV input and output."}, {"title": "DensityProfile.load", "href": "api-data.html#densityprofile-load", "text": "panda_md.DensityProfile.load "}, {"title": "DensityProfile.save", "href": "api-data.html#densityprofile-save", "text": "panda_md.DensityProfile.save Save: .npz \u2014 everything; .csv \u2014 columns and metadata in comment lines."}, {"title": "DensityProfile.mean_density_per_nm3", "href": "api-data.html#densityprofile-mean_density_per_nm3", "text": "panda_md.DensityProfile.mean_density_per_nm3 n\u0304 = N / V \u2014 mean density of the liquid in the pore."}, {"title": "ProfileSet", "href": "api-data.html#profileset", "text": "panda_md.ProfileSet One or more profiles on a common bin grid. The time bounds and frame counts describe the samples contributing to each block. Use NPZ to persist the set."}, {"title": "ProfileSet.load", "href": "api-data.html#profileset-load", "text": "panda_md.ProfileSet.load "}, {"title": "ProfileSet.save", "href": "api-data.html#profileset-save", "text": "panda_md.ProfileSet.save Save to .npz (arrays and metadata)."}, {"title": "ProfileSet.mean", "href": "api-data.html#profileset-mean", "text": "panda_md.ProfileSet.mean Return the mean over blocks."}, {"title": "ProfileSet.block", "href": "api-data.html#profileset-block", "text": "panda_md.ProfileSet.block "}, {"title": "ProfileSet.std", "href": "api-data.html#profileset-std", "text": "panda_md.ProfileSet.std Standard deviation of the density over blocks (0 for a single block)."}, {"title": "ProfileSet.sem", "href": "api-data.html#profileset-sem", "text": "panda_md.ProfileSet.sem Standard error of the mean over blocks: std / \u221a(number of blocks)."}, {"title": "ProfileSet.block_count", "href": "api-data.html#profileset-block_count", "text": "panda_md.ProfileSet.block_count Number of available profiles or time blocks."}, {"title": "ProfileSet.coordinate_nm", "href": "api-data.html#profileset-coordinate_nm", "text": "panda_md.ProfileSet.coordinate_nm Common bin centers in nm."}, {"title": "density_map", "href": "api-data.html#density_map", "text": "panda_md.density_map Compute a two-dimensional number-density map in a slit pore. A supported shape name enables alignment on the shape symmetry axis."}, {"title": "DensityMap", "href": "api-data.html#densitymap", "text": "panda_md.DensityMap Binned two-dimensional number density in nm\u207b\u00b3 and its bin edges in nm."}, {"title": "fit_blocks", "href": "api-analysis.html#fit_blocks", "text": "panda_md.fit_blocks Fit each block of a ProfileSet with the same model and settings."}, {"title": "FitResultSet", "href": "api-analysis.html#fitresultset", "text": "panda_md.FitResultSet Per-block fits and summary statistics. Interpret SEM as uncertainty of the mean only when blocks are sufficiently independent."}, {"title": "FitResultSet.values", "href": "api-analysis.html#fitresultset-values", "text": "panda_md.FitResultSet.values Value of the parameter (user units) in each block."}, {"title": "FitResultSet.mean", "href": "api-analysis.html#fitresultset-mean", "text": "panda_md.FitResultSet.mean Return the mean over blocks."}, {"title": "FitResultSet.std", "href": "api-analysis.html#fitresultset-std", "text": "panda_md.FitResultSet.std Spread over blocks; not defined (nan) for a single block."}, {"title": "FitResultSet.sem", "href": "api-analysis.html#fitresultset-sem", "text": "panda_md.FitResultSet.sem Standard error of the mean: std / \u221a(number of blocks) \u2014 valid if the blocks exceed the correlation time."}, {"title": "FitResultSet.summary", "href": "api-analysis.html#fitresultset-summary", "text": "panda_md.FitResultSet.summary Return a human-readable summary of the result and its diagnostics."}, {"title": "statistical_inefficiency", "href": "api-analysis.html#statistical_inefficiency", "text": "panda_md.statistical_inefficiency Estimate how the variance of block means changes with block length for a series."}, {"title": "StatisticalInefficiency", "href": "api-analysis.html#statisticalinefficiency", "text": "panda_md.StatisticalInefficiency Block lengths and estimated inefficiencies, with a plateau estimate when enough reliable lengths exist."}, {"title": "StatisticalInefficiency.plateau", "href": "api-analysis.html#statisticalinefficiency-plateau", "text": "panda_md.StatisticalInefficiency.plateau Mean s over the last third of the lengths with at least MIN_BLOCKS blocks (otherwise over the last third"}, {"title": "compare_shapes", "href": "api-analysis.html#compare_shapes", "text": "panda_md.compare_shapes Fit candidate shapes to the same profile and rank by loss. The result retains skipped shapes and records nearly indistinguishable candidates."}, {"title": "ShapeComparison", "href": "api-analysis.html#shapecomparison", "text": "panda_md.ShapeComparison Comparison of feasible fits and skipped candidates."}, {"title": "ShapeComparison.fitted", "href": "api-analysis.html#shapecomparison-fitted", "text": "panda_md.ShapeComparison.fitted Successful candidate fits, in ranking order."}, {"title": "ShapeComparison.best", "href": "api-analysis.html#shapecomparison-best", "text": "panda_md.ShapeComparison.best The lowest-loss fitted candidate."}, {"title": "ShapeComparison.indistinguishable", "href": "api-analysis.html#shapecomparison-indistinguishable", "text": "panda_md.ShapeComparison.indistinguishable Feasible shapes with a loss at most LOSS_TIE_FRACTION above the best: the profile cannot tell them apart."}, {"title": "ShapeComparison.summary", "href": "api-analysis.html#shapecomparison-summary", "text": "panda_md.ShapeComparison.summary Return a human-readable summary of the result and its diagnostics."}, {"title": "ShapeFit", "href": "api-analysis.html#shapefit", "text": "panda_md.ShapeFit One candidate's fit result or the reason PANDA skipped it."}, {"title": "stability_diagram", "href": "api-analysis.html#stability_diagram", "text": "panda_md.stability_diagram Find the minimum capillary energy over volume fractions and reduced pore lengths at a fixed angle and wall-layer thickness."}, {"title": "StabilityDiagram", "href": "api-analysis.html#stabilitydiagram", "text": "panda_md.StabilityDiagram Grid of stable shape names, indexed by length ratio then volume fraction. None means no candidate exists at that point."}, {"title": "synthetic_profile", "href": "api-synthetic.html#synthetic_profile", "text": "panda_md.synthetic_profile Generate a one-dimensional profile for known model parameters. Set seed for repeatable noise."}, {"title": "synthetic_trajectory", "href": "api-synthetic.html#synthetic_trajectory", "text": "panda_md.synthetic_trajectory Sample particle coordinates for a slit-pore shape that implements point containment. The returned trajectory includes liquid and walls groups."}, {"title": "AccuracyCase", "href": "api-synthetic.html#accuracycase", "text": "panda_md.analysis.accuracy.AccuracyCase Configuration for one synthetic recovery case, including the input parameters and noise settings."}, {"title": "angle_errors", "href": "api-synthetic.html#angle_errors", "text": "panda_md.analysis.accuracy.angle_errors Repeat a synthetic fit with independent seeds and collect fitted-angle errors."}, {"title": "AngleErrors", "href": "api-synthetic.html#angleerrors", "text": "panda_md.analysis.accuracy.AngleErrors Per-seed errors in degrees (fitted minus input) and flags for fits at the angle bound."}, {"title": "accuracy_study", "href": "api-synthetic.html#accuracy_study", "text": "panda_md.analysis.accuracy.accuracy_study Run a collection of synthetic recovery cases."}, {"title": "AccuracyStudy", "href": "api-synthetic.html#accuracystudy", "text": "panda_md.analysis.accuracy.AccuracyStudy Collect case-by-case angle errors for tables or figures."}, {"title": "AccuracyStudy.mean_absolute", "href": "api-synthetic.html#accuracystudy-mean_absolute", "text": "panda_md.analysis.accuracy.AccuracyStudy.mean_absolute "}, {"title": "AccuracyStudy.maximum_absolute", "href": "api-synthetic.html#accuracystudy-maximum_absolute", "text": "panda_md.analysis.accuracy.AccuracyStudy.maximum_absolute "}, {"title": "AccuracyStudy.bias", "href": "api-synthetic.html#accuracystudy-bias", "text": "panda_md.analysis.accuracy.AccuracyStudy.bias Systematic shift: the mean of (recovered \u2212 true)."}, {"title": "AccuracyStudy.table", "href": "api-synthetic.html#accuracystudy-table", "text": "panda_md.analysis.accuracy.AccuracyStudy.table Format the accuracy metrics as a text table."}, {"title": "NoiseModel", "href": "api-synthetic.html#noisemodel", "text": "panda_md.core.enums.NoiseModel Noise model for a synthetic density profile."}, {"title": "ProfileSampling", "href": "api-synthetic.html#profilesampling", "text": "panda_md.core.enums.ProfileSampling Use the center of each bin or average the model across the bin."}, {"title": "plot_profile", "href": "api-plotting.html#plot_profile", "text": "panda_md.plotting.plot_profile Draw one density profile or a mean with block-based standard errors."}, {"title": "plot_fit", "href": "api-plotting.html#plot_fit", "text": "panda_md.plotting.plot_fit Overlay normalized data and the fitted curve on the fit coordinate."}, {"title": "plot_blocks", "href": "api-plotting.html#plot_blocks", "text": "panda_md.plotting.plot_blocks Draw one fitted parameter at the midpoint of each time block."}, {"title": "plot_density_map", "href": "api-plotting.html#plot_density_map", "text": "panda_md.plotting.plot_density_map Render a slit-pore number-density map with a colorbar."}, {"title": "plot_stability", "href": "api-plotting.html#plot_stability", "text": "panda_md.plotting.plot_stability Render stable morphologies on the volume-fraction and reduced-length grid."}, {"title": "plot_accuracy", "href": "api-plotting.html#plot_accuracy", "text": "panda_md.plotting.plot_accuracy Visualize angle errors across synthetic recovery cases."}, {"title": "save_fit_figure", "href": "api-plotting.html#save_fit_figure", "text": "panda_md.plotting.save_fit_figure Export the fit figure to a file. Its extension determines the format."}, {"title": "supported_figure_formats", "href": "api-plotting.html#supported_figure_formats", "text": "panda_md.plotting.supported_figure_formats List formats supported by the Matplotlib writer."}, {"title": "Axis", "href": "api-types.html#axis", "text": "panda_md.Axis Cartesian axis of the rectangular simulation box."}, {"title": "Axis.column", "href": "api-types.html#axis-column", "text": "panda_md.Axis.column Column index of the coordinate in the position array (x \u2014 0, y \u2014 1, z \u2014 2)."}, {"title": "AxisLocator", "href": "api-types.html#axislocator", "text": "panda_md.AxisLocator Rule for locating the symmetry axis within a frame."}, {"title": "AxisOrientation", "href": "api-types.html#axisorientation", "text": "panda_md.AxisOrientation Direction of a shape symmetry axis relative to the walls."}, {"title": "Frame", "href": "api-types.html#frame", "text": "panda_md.Frame Coordinate frame in which the density profile is expressed."}, {"title": "LossFunction", "href": "api-types.html#lossfunction", "text": "panda_md.LossFunction Mean absolute or mean squared deviation between profiles."}, {"title": "Normalization", "href": "api-types.html#normalization", "text": "panda_md.Normalization Choice of bulk or mean density normalization."}, {"title": "OptimizerMethod", "href": "api-types.html#optimizermethod", "text": "panda_md.OptimizerMethod Local optimizer used by the fit."}, {"title": "Orientation", "href": "api-types.html#orientation", "text": "panda_md.Orientation Whether pore-frame profiles can be reflected along the normal axis."}, {"title": "ParameterName", "href": "api-types.html#parametername", "text": "panda_md.ParameterName Standard keys in result values and fit settings."}, {"title": "ParticleGrouping", "href": "api-types.html#particlegrouping", "text": "panda_md.ParticleGrouping Count selected atoms or centers of mass of molecules."}, {"title": "ProfileCentering", "href": "api-types.html#profilecentering", "text": "panda_md.ProfileCentering Reference point placed at zero for each profile."}, {"title": "Regime", "href": "api-types.html#regime", "text": "panda_md.Regime Wetting or non-wetting regime of the selected liquid."}, {"title": "Unit", "href": "api-types.html#unit", "text": "panda_md.Unit Unit convention used for a model parameter."}, {"title": "PandaError", "href": "api-types.html#pandaerror", "text": "panda_md.PandaError Base exception for errors reported by PANDA."}, {"title": "PandaWarning", "href": "api-types.html#pandawarning", "text": "panda_md.PandaWarning Base warning emitted for diagnostic conditions."}, {"title": "InfeasibleParametersError", "href": "api-types.html#infeasibleparameterserror", "text": "panda_md.InfeasibleParametersError The parameters do not admit the requested morphology."}, {"title": "InvalidProfileError", "href": "api-types.html#invalidprofileerror", "text": "panda_md.InvalidProfileError The input density profile is invalid or lacks required metadata."}, {"title": "InvalidTrajectoryError", "href": "api-types.html#invalidtrajectoryerror", "text": "panda_md.InvalidTrajectoryError The trajectory, frame selection, or box geometry is invalid for the requested operation."}, {"title": "MissingDependencyError", "href": "api-types.html#missingdependencyerror", "text": "panda_md.MissingDependencyError An optional package required by the requested operation is missing."}, {"title": "NotDerivedError", "href": "api-types.html#notderivederror", "text": "panda_md.NotDerivedError The requested analytical operation has no implementation for this shape or pore."}, {"title": "ProfileMismatchError", "href": "api-types.html#profilemismatcherror", "text": "panda_md.ProfileMismatchError The input profile and model are incompatible."}, {"title": "UnsupportedRegimeError", "href": "api-types.html#unsupportedregimeerror", "text": "panda_md.UnsupportedRegimeError The requested wetting regime is unavailable for the model."}, {"title": "__version__", "href": "api-types.html#__version__", "text": "panda_md.__version__ Installed package version string."}];
